<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE TRAILING SLOT'S OPTICAL PULL — view_row.xml's five trailing glyphs.
  ============================================================================

  A file of its own and not an addition to values/dimens.xml, because these
  numbers belong to the universal row alone: nothing else may reach for them, and
  none of them is a spacing step.

  This is ToolbarBinder.alignInkToGutter's problem again, one component down, and
  it takes the same answer: what the eye lines a column up by is the GLYPH's last
  painted pixel, never the edge of the invisible box it is centred in.

  THE LINE THEY LINE UP ON IS THE ROW'S OWN 16dp GUTTER, and getting THAT wrong is
  what brought the owner back a third time. The slot held five objects at five
  distances, so the first round measured them all and put the two icon-action
  glyphs level with the CHEVRON, at 22dp. It closed the gap between them and left
  every one of them 6dp adrift of the line the rest of the row is measured to:
  @style/Widget.Departament.Row's paddingEnd is @dimen/screen_gutter, 16, which is
  where the text column ends, where the card's content edge is, and the ONE gutter
  CLAUDE.md gives the product. The chevron had the defect too — it was simply the
  one nobody could see, because it never stood beside anything to be compared with.
  On «О приложении» the copy buttons share a card with it and he saw it at once:
  «выше где кнопки копировать справа тоже видишь ты не доделал, надо их правее
  также поставить правильно».

  So the datum is not a control any more, it is the gutter, and every trailing
  glyph's INK ends on it.

  ONLY GLYPHS ARE PULLED. @id/row_check_box, @id/row_switch and @id/row_action are
  objects with a boundary of their own — a bordered box, a track, a button — and an
  object aligns by its box, exactly as a card does. A bare glyph has no boundary,
  so its ink IS its edge. That is the whole rule, and it is why three of the eight
  trailing slots are absent from this file.

  MEASURED OFF THE DRAWABLES, NOT GUESSED. Every glyph the slot ever holds is a
  24-unit viewport; an ImageView at @dimen/glyph_18 fitCenters it to 18dp (× 0.75)
  and the icon button draws it at @dimen/tile_glyph 22dp (× 0.9167). Air is what is
  left between the last painted unit and the viewport's trailing edge:

                        ink x    air (units)   drawn at   air (dp)   pull
      ic_chevron_right  7.2…16        8          18dp       6.00     -6.00
      ic_arrow_drop_down  7…17        7          18dp       5.25     -5.25
      ic_action_done      3…21        3          18dp       2.25     -2.25
      ic_copy             2…21        3          22dp       2.75     -9.75  (+7 box)
      ic_more_vert_24dp  10…14       10          22dp       9.17    -16.00  (+7 box)

  ONE NUMBER CANNOT SERVE THEM, which is the trap the toolbar hit first: «⋮» is a
  4-unit column of dots in a 24-unit box and «копировать» is a 19-unit frame in
  one. A single shared pull big enough for the chevron would hang the state marker
  3.75dp past the gutter, into the padding. The correction belongs to the GLYPH.

  WHERE EACH PULL IS APPLIED FOLLOWS FROM WHO CHOOSES THE GLYPH. @id/row_chevron
  and @id/row_marker declare their own `android:src` in view_row.xml, so their pull
  is a static `layout_marginEnd` three lines under the drawable it was measured
  from, and no recycled row can carry the wrong one. @id/row_trailing_glyph ships
  with no src on purpose and @id/row_icon_action's icon is the caller's, so those
  two are pulled at bind time by RowBinder.alignInkToGutter — the one place that
  knows which glyph is going in — and a glyph it has never seen is reset to NO
  pull rather than to a guess.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
        THE ICON BUTTON'S BOX, and the number that made this round different from
        the last one.

        @id/row_icon_action is not an ImageView: it is a MaterialButton carrying the
        48dp touch minimum, so its 22dp icon sits in 13dp of air on each side. Its
        ink cannot reach the gutter by moving — «⋮» would need -22.17, and the last
        6.17 of that is outside the row, where the box is clipped and the press
        plate is sheared off. Moving a glyph by shearing its plate is a defect the
        owner has already reported once, on Главная's chevron.

        So the box stops moving and SHRINKS. 36 is the size the подписка card's
        action discs already draw at (layout_subscription_meta_bar.xml's
        «Проверить», «Обновить», «Telegram»), which makes it the product's one small
        icon-button size rather than a sixth number, and it is the largest box that
        keeps «⋮» inside the row: 22 + 2 × (16 − 9.17) = 35.67, rounded to the
        shipped 36 and taken up by the pull below. The 22dp glyph keeps a 7dp plate
        around it — the copy frame's corners sit at radius 12.3 and the disc's is
        18, so nothing pokes out of the plate, which a 22dp box would not have
        managed.

        THE 48dp TARGET IS NOT GIVEN UP, it stops being drawn (00-rules.md 14.2).
        RowBinder restores it with the TouchDelegate the подписка discs use.

        It also takes 12dp off two rows that were never meant to be tall: a 48dp box
        is 8dp taller than the 40dp tile, so «Версия» and «Идентификатор» on
        «О приложении» stood at 68dp beside 60dp neighbours, and every «Файлы
        ресурсов» line at 68 instead of the prototype's 61. Same cause as
        3aedd33e's switch, one slot over: a touch minimum drawn as a box.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_action_size">36dp</dimen>

    <!--
        ic_copy at 22dp: 7dp of box air plus 2.75dp of its own.
        16 − 7 − 2.75 = 6.25, so the ink lands on 16.00 exactly and the plate still
        clears the card's edge by 6.25 — a quarter of a dp off the 6 that
        @dimen/optical_nudge_touch_target leaves on the leading side of the
        subscription card, which is the shipped precedent for this shape.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_action_nudge_wide">-9.75dp</dimen>

    <!--
        ic_more_vert_24dp at 22dp: 7dp of box air plus 9.17dp of its own, so the
        exact pull is -16.17 and this is the one glyph in the file that is CLAMPED.

        SIXTEEN IS THE ROW'S WHOLE END GUTTER and this control gives all of it back:
        the glyph is so narrow that its box has to travel the full padding for the
        ink to reach the line. Stopping at -16 leaves the ink at 16.17 — a sixth of
        a dp, half a pixel at 3× — and keeps the box FLUSH with the row's edge
        instead of 0.17 outside it, which is the difference between a plate that is
        tangent and a plate that is shorn. view_toolbar.xml settled the same
        question on the other side: «the target reaching the screen edge is a
        Fitts's-law gain rather than a cost». The plate's widest point is at the
        row's vertical centre, well clear of the card's 20dp corners.

        This is also the owner's standing request on this glyph, already honoured in
        the toolbar: «три точки которые сверху справа их бы тоже чутка правее
        сделать и это касается везде где они есть».
    -->
    <dimen name="row_action_nudge_overflow">-16dp</dimen>

    <!--
        THE THREE 18dp GLYPH SLOTS. Their boxes already end on the gutter, so the
        pull is nothing but the glyph's own air: 8, 7 and 3 units of a 24-unit
        viewport, at × 0.75.

        The chevron is the biggest of the three because ic_chevron_right is drawn
        inside a 24-unit box that also has to hold the arrow's other three sides.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_glyph_nudge_chevron">-6dp</dimen>

    <!--
        ic_arrow_drop_down, the cycle caret. Its ink is symmetric about the box
        centre (7…17 of 24), so SelectPopup turning it 180° while the popup is open
        does not move the edge this number was measured from.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_glyph_nudge_caret">-5.25dp</dimen>

    <!--
        ic_action_done, the state marker. The smallest pull in the file: the tick
        very nearly fills its viewport, which is exactly why one shared number could
        never have served all three.
    -->
    <dimen name="row_glyph_nudge_check">-2.25dp</dimen>

</resources>
